        page["route"] = "/doc/api/string-list/"
        page["title"] = "StringList"
        page["content"] = "Use a list-shaped `dval` for an ordered string list in Capy. Create one with `dval([...])` or use a result from `split`, `split_utf8`, `regex_split`, `ls`, `units_list`, or `request.websocket.connections` in a `WS` handler.\n\nList functions take a list-shaped `dval` and return a `dval`, a `string`, or a `bool`. Use `join`, `map`, `filter`, `keys`, `unique`, `sort`, `some`, `every`, and `string_list_find` for normal list work.\n\n`dval_push` and `dval_pop` mutate the target list and return that same identity. Assigning the result back remains valid.\n\n## Capy Limit\n\nCapy has no separate `StringList` type or representation. It uses mutable DValue reference values inside a workspace. A C++ boundary copies BRRB and does not expose a container alias.\n\n## C++ API\n\n`StringList` is a C++ name for a list-shaped `DValue`. Capy uses a list-shaped `dval` instead.\n"
